    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **258 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including both new acceptance tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner response so that it returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise.\n\nThe change follows existing Spring/OpenAPI conventions in the repo, where derived read-only fields are declared in the OpenAPI spec and computed in the MapStruct mapper (like `displayName` and `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` property (string enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` schema, so the code generator produces the DTO field and its `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression that computes the tier from the owner's persisted `namesakeCount` and `email`:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank)\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise\n\nComputing it in the mapper (rather than persisting it) means the value is correctly derived on every `GET /api/owners/{id}` read, which is what the acceptance tests exercise.",
